bio:
Partner at Webber Newdigate &amp; Webbers Attorneys · I am a practicing Attorney. My scope of influence has for the past five years been focused mainly on employment law. I have an extensive experience in handling cases for employers in all the labour dispute resolution forums in Lesotho; I have also done two training sessions for two transnational retail companies focusing on local labour law compliance; chairing disciplinary hearings; sometimes I represent employers in disciplinary hearing where lawyers have to participate; reviewing and drafting employment contracts and Human Resource policies/manuals; and advising clients on labour matters in general. 

But I also work in the following practice areas: 

•	High Court General litigation; 
•	Magistrate’s Court general litigation; 
•	Land Court litigation; 
•	Drafting wills, administration of deceased estates; 
•	Registration of land title use, bonds, sublease agreements; 

